# Netlify / Cloudflare Pages redirect rules.
#
# "PC repair {city}" and "computer repair {city}" are the same search intent.
# Two separate pages would compete with each other for the same queries and split
# the link equity — classic keyword cannibalization. One strong page wins both,
# so every /pc-repair/* URL 301s into its /computer-repair/* equivalent.
# 301 (not 302) because it permanently passes ranking signals to the target.
/pc-repair/*        /computer-repair/:splat        301
/laptop-repair/*    /computer-repair/:splat        301
/computer-repair    /locations                     301
/services/index     /services                      301

# Canonical host. Serving both www and non-www as 200 is duplicate content and
# splits your ranking signal across two hostnames. Pick one and 301 the other.
# Uncomment the line matching your choice — non-www is the default below.
https://www.cleanfeatures.com/*   https://cleanfeatures.com/:splat   301!
# https://cleanfeatures.com/*     https://www.cleanfeatures.com/:splat  301!
